keel-web (0.1.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * First release (handbook decision 0041, first implementation, step 7).
    Ships the appliance manifest of Keel Web from docs/manifest-v1.md as
    /usr/share/keel/appliances/web.yaml: Core plus nginx, enabled in every
    mode, and coraza and anubis, disabled in simple and enabled in the
    cloud modes. Web has no process of its own.
  * Ships /etc/nginx/sites-available/default-anubis, Debian's default site
    behind Anubis, and /usr/lib/keel/overlays/anubis/state.d/50keel-web,
    which keel spec apply runs when the anubis overlay is turned on or
    off: it puts that front in place of Debian's default site, and back,
    tested with nginx -t and reloaded, and leaves an edited default site
    alone. The socket Anubis reads is served without gzip, which also
    keeps its pages whole while Coraza is on
    (Keel-Linux/libnginx-mod-http-coraza#2).
  * Depends on keel-core, the three Web overlays and keel (>= 0.15.0), the
    first keel that runs the overlays' state hooks.

